# Line endings are normalized to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: dozens of guards in this repo are *structural tests over
# source text* — they read files such as `app/Sources/**/*.swift`, `scripts/*.js`
# and `shared/*.md` and assert on their content with LF-anchored patterns. With no
# `.gitattributes`, a Windows checkout under the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# hands those guards CRLF and they break for a reason that has nothing to do with
# the property under test (measured: converting the 58 sources under `app/Sources`
# to CRLF reproduces the exact Windows CI failures; restoring LF makes them pass).
#
# Scope check performed before writing this rule: an in-process scan of all 544
# tracked files found **zero** files containing CRLF and zero containing a lone CR.
# The repo's deliberate CRLF fixtures (PR #85, plan files in CRLF/BOM) are built at
# test runtime under a temp dir — they are never tracked, so this rule cannot reach
# them. Should a CRLF fixture ever need to be committed, exclude it explicitly here
# with `-text` (or `eol=crlf`) rather than weakening the blanket rule.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by EOL conversion.
*.icns binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
